24,37018,90,66,61,19,15170,7,66,481,264,2376,66,481,293,2376,66,481,294,2376,66,481,384,9139,488,1124,37018,90,67,61,19,15170,7,67,481,264,2376,67,481,293,2376,67,481,272,2376,67,481,384,9139,90155,5,59,31610,488,1124,37018,90,68,61,19,15170,7,68,481,264,2376,68,481,293,2376,68,481,272,2376,68,481,294,9139,624,59,408,90,6612,9,92,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ $d,$ and $e$ be the distinct roots of the equation $x^5 + 7x^4 - 2 = 0.$  Find\n\\begin{align*}\n&\\frac{a^4}{(a - b)(a - c)(a - d)(a - e)} + \\frac{b^4}{(b - a)(b - c)(b - d)(b - e)} \\\\\n&\\quad + \\frac{c^4}{(c - a)(c - b)(c - d)(c - e)} + \\frac{d^4}{(d - a)(d - b)(d - c)(d - e)} \\\\\n&\\quad + \\frac{e^4}{(e - a)(e - b)(e - c)(e - d)}.\n\\end{align*}","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"175283ef9db316cebac0e7ac39fac6f9f931df72facfd7e88e41c3ee8220735e"},"seconds":44.32491874694824,"seed":787709645423857001,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the given problem, we will make use of properties of polynomials and their roots. Let \\( P(x) = x^5 + 7x^4 - 2 \\). The roots of \\( P(x) \\) are \\( a, b, c, d, \\) and \\( e \\). We need to evaluate the expression\n\n\\[\nS = \\frac{a^4}{(a - b)(a - c)(a - d)(a - e)} + \\frac{b^4}{(b - a)(b - c)(b - d)(b - e)} + \\frac{c^4}{(c - a)(c - b)(c - d)(c - e)} + \\frac{d^4}{(d - a)(d - b)(d - c)(d - e)} + \\frac{e^4}{(e - a)(e - b)(e - c)(e - d)}.\n\\]\n\nTo proceed, consider the polynomial \\( P(x) \\) and the Lagrange interpolation formula. The polynomial \\( P(x) \\) can be written as:\n\n\\[\nP(x) = (x - a)(x - b)(x - c)(x - d)(x - e).\n\\]\n\nGiven the polynomial \\( P(x) = x^5 + 7x^4 - 2 \\), we need to evaluate a sum of terms involving the roots. We use the fact that the polynomial can be expressed in terms of its roots and the coefficients of the polynomial.\n\nConsider the polynomial \\( Q(x) = \\frac{P(x)}{x - r} \\) for each root \\( r \\). Each \\( Q(x) \\) is a polynomial of degree 4, and we are interested in the value of \\( Q(r) \\) at each root \\( r \\).\n\nBy the properties of the polynomial and its roots, we have the following:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{P(x)}{(x - a)(x - b)(x - c)(x - d)(x - e)} = 1.\n\\]\n\nThis implies that the polynomial \\( P(x) \\) can be expressed in terms of its roots as:\n\n\\[\nP(x) = (x - a)(x - b)(x - c)(x - d)(x - e).\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to evaluate the sum:\n\n\\[\nS = \\sum_{\\text{cyc}} \\frac{a^4}{(a - b)(a - c)(a - d)(a - e)}.\n\\]\n\nBy the properties of symmetric sums and the polynomial \\( P(x) \\), we can use the fact that the sum of the residues of the polynomial at its roots is given by the coefficient of the polynomial. Specifically, the sum of the residues of the polynomial \\( \\frac{x^4}{P'(x)} \\) at its roots is equal to the coefficient of the \\( x^4 \\) term in the polynomial \\( P(x) \\) divided by the leading coefficient.\n\nGiven that the polynomial \\( P(x) \\) is \\( x^5 + 7x^4 - 2 \\), the coefficient of \\( x^4 \\) is 7. Therefore, the sum of the residues is:\n\n\\[\nS = 1.\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of the given expression is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{1}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
